# Naming Conventions

## Files and Classes

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Screen | `*Screen.kt` | `ChatScreen.kt`, `MessagesScreen.kt` |
| ViewModel | `*ViewModel.kt` | `ChatViewModel.kt` |
| Store | `*Store.kt` | `MessageStore.kt`, `DirectStore.kt` |
| Repository | `*Repository.kt` | `ChatRepository.kt` |
| Entity/Model | `*Entity.kt` or descriptive | `MessageEntity.kt`, `DirectMessage.kt` |
| UiState | `*UiState` (sealed interface) | `ChatUiState`, `MessagesUiState` |
| Intent | `*Intent` (sealed interface) | `ChatIntent`, `LoginIntent` |
| Event | `*Event` (sealed interface) | `LoginEvent` |

## Proto mapping extensions

Place in the same file as the target entity:

```kotlin
fun ChannelMessage.toMessageEntity(currentUserId: Long): MessageEntity = ...
fun ChannelDescription.toDirectMessage(currentUserId: Long): DirectMessage = ...
```

## File organization

Group by feature folder:

```
home/
  chat/        → ChatScreen, ChatViewModel, ChatRepository, MessageStore, MessageEntity
  messages/    → MessagesScreen, MessagesViewModel, DirectRepository, DirectStore, DirectMessage
  clans/       → ClansScreen, ...
  profile/     → ProfileScreen, ProfileViewModel
```
